   described as "read-only over every input except this one, single,
   idempotent, lock-guarded consumption update," never as unconditionally
   read-only, and never as a general-purpose ledger-mutating process.
+
+#### Human-attended issuance broker
+
+`issue-live-host-challenge.py --matrix-cell CELL --issuer-key-id KEY_ID
+--nonce-ledger PATH --trusted-signers PATH` accepts only the five existing
+matrix-cell literals and existing regular repository files. It provides no
+caller override for nonce, timestamp, issuer, schema, signer command, or key
+material. It invokes the canonical A1 Python entry point with fixed argv and
+`--emit-challenge`; `shell=True`, alternate executables, and imported or
+handwritten challenge JSON are forbidden.
+
+The broker derives `issued_at` in UTC and preserves the existing literal
+`issuer: check-hook-activation-handshake` as the nonce-generator identifier.
+It displays the existing unsigned five-field ledger entry and the existing
+domain-separated digest, then reads exactly one canonical base64 Ed25519
+signature line from the attending human. It neither reads nor launches a
+private-key operation. Before append it re-reads and re-validates the registry
+and full ledger, rejects duplicate nonce or registry drift, enforces the
+24-hour wall-clock and monotonic deadline, and verifies the signature against
+the registered issuer-role public key.
+
+Issuance and consumption share `PATH + ".lock"`. Under that lock the broker
+re-reads the latest ledger, appends one entry with `consumed_by_record: null`,
+and uses the validator's existing same-directory temp, fsync, and atomic-replace
+discipline. It never removes another process's lock. stdout is empty until the
+append is durable; only then does it emit the unchanged A1 challenge JSON.
+Failure before append leaves the ledger byte-identical. Failure while emitting
+stdout after append leaves the entry durable and forbids replay, deletion, or
+re-output; recovery is a fresh issuance. Exit categories are 0 durable issuance,
+2 input/schema, 3 trust/signature, 4 lock/storage, 5 A1 generation, and
+6 expiry/interruption. None is a native verdict, two-party live-host record,
+approval, or AC-028 discharge.
